        <div class="sg-group" id="card-hover">
          <h3 class="sg-group-heading">Card hover — <code>.card-float</code></h3>
          <p class="sg-section__desc">
            The one hover language for every whole-card <em>link</em>: the card rises
            <code>--card-float-lift</code>, swells <code>--card-float-scale</code>, and its
            shadow grows one step up the scale — a physical card lifting off the surface and
            coming nearer the eye. Set the resting shadow with
            <code>--card-float-shadow</code> (never a scoped <code>box-shadow</code> — it would
            outrank the utility) and the raised one with
            <code>--card-float-shadow-hover</code>. A card that is <em>not</em> itself a click
            target must not carry it: the gesture is the affordance. Hover each.
          </p>
          <div class="sg-cardfloat-grid">
            <a href="#card-hover" class="sg-cardfloat card-float">
              <strong>Flat card</strong>
              <span>no shadow &rarr; <code>--shadow-md</code></span>
              <span class="sg-cardfloat__note">defaults — just add the class (PostCard, LinkCard)</span>
