            <div slot="panel-1">
              <StepList steps={[
                { title: 'Launch a Secure Datasite', body: 'Stand up a datasite to make your data available for approved research without exposing it.' },
                { title: 'Review Research Proposals', body: 'Inspect the code researchers submit before anything runs against your data.' },
                { title: 'Approve compliant projects', body: 'Approve the projects that meet your policies; results are returned, raw data stays put.' },
              ]} />
            </div>
          </Tabs>
        </div>

        <div class="sg-group" id="accordion">
          <h3 class="sg-group-heading">Accordion — native &lt;details&gt; disclosure (stack for an FAQ)</h3>
          <div class="sg-accordion-stack">
            <Accordion title="How does Syft ensure the analysis doesn’t reveal personal or protected information?" open>
              <p>Syft preserves data privacy by enabling data scientists to study data without ever seeing or copying it — code is sent to the data and only approved results are returned.</p>
            </Accordion>
            <Accordion title="What security measures does Syft implement?">
              <p>Access is mediated by per-datasite policies, request review, and an immutable audit log of every approved computation.</p>
            </Accordion>
            <Accordion title="Where else is Syft deployed?">
              <p>Across research consortia, public institutions, and enterprises collaborating on sensitive data.</p>
            </Accordion>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ICONS -->
      <section class="sg-section" id="icons">
        <h2 class="sg-section__title">Icons</h2>

        <div class="sg-group" id="hosted-icons">
          <h3 class="sg-group-heading">Hosted — local SVG set ({hostedIcons.length})</h3>
          <p class="sg-section__desc">
            The complete set we ship: inlined from <code>src/assets/icons/</code> via
            <code>&lt;Icon name="…" /&gt;</code> (<code>@elements/Icon</code>). No CDN — they paint
            with the document and take <code>currentColor</code>. Grouped by role — Interface (wired
            into controls), Content (a-la-carte editorial), Brand logos (third-party). Content is the
            computed remainder, so a newly added icon always shows up. Reference every page/element
            icon by name from here.
          </p>
          {iconGroups.map((group) => (
            <div class="sg-icon-group">
              <h4 class="sg-icon-group__title">{group.name} <span class="text-caption">({group.names.length})</span></h4>
              <p class="sg-icon-group__desc text-caption">{group.desc}</p>
              <div class="sg-icon-grid">
                {group.names.map((name) => (
                  <div class="sg-icon-cell">
                    <Icon name={name} size={28} />
                    <span class="text-caption">{name}</span>
                  </div>
                ))}
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
